# twin: render_one
# One console that asks for an OpenGL ES 2 context and draws the two-part
# picture in the one it gets, which a driver may make of a later version:
# its framebuffer has neither depth nor stencil, and the picture starts at
# the framebuffer's first row. On llvmpipe check-gl runs it once more in a
# context held to version 2.0.
console 0 core=test render=gl
option 0 link_test_render gl
option 0 link_test_gl_context gles2
option 0 link_test_gl_origin bottom
30 checkpoint early
60 save mid
60 checkpoint mid
120 end
